1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,550
You can send a photo

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:03,720
around the world in a second.

3
00:00:03,779 --> 00:00:05,699
So why can buying into a fund

4
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:08,529
still take two business days to settle?

5
00:00:08,799 --> 00:00:10,719
Because the money sits in one place,

6
00:00:10,739 --> 00:00:12,499
and the record of who owns what

7
00:00:12,519 --> 00:00:13,808
sits in another.

8
00:00:13,828 --> 00:00:16,068
Different firms keep their own copies,

9
00:00:16,088 --> 00:00:18,238
and someone has to check they match.

10
00:00:18,612 --> 00:00:20,312
Redbelly is a public network,

11
00:00:20,332 --> 00:00:21,492
built in Australia,

12
00:00:21,512 --> 00:00:23,159
that brings the two together.

13
00:00:23,179 --> 00:00:25,877
Payment and ownership move in one step.

14
00:00:25,897 --> 00:00:28,658
If either side fails, nothing moves.

15
00:00:28,678 --> 00:00:31,128
Once it's done, it's final.

16
00:00:31,525 --> 00:00:33,402
And it's not a free-for-all.

17
00:00:33,422 --> 00:00:35,162
The people trading are verified,

18
00:00:35,182 --> 00:00:37,322
a bit like showing ID at a bank,

19
00:00:37,342 --> 00:00:39,832
and their private details stay protected.

20
00:00:40,135 --> 00:00:42,207
The rules are built in too.

21
00:00:42,227 --> 00:00:44,167
Before a trade goes through,

22
00:00:44,187 --> 00:00:44,887
the system checks

23
00:00:44,907 --> 00:00:46,821
the buyer is allowed to buy it.

24
00:00:46,841 --> 00:00:49,311
If not, it simply doesn't happen.

25
00:00:49,713 --> 00:00:51,733
So things like property, loans,

26
00:00:51,753 --> 00:00:53,093
bonds and investment funds

27
00:00:53,113 --> 00:00:54,993
can be issued and traded digitally,

28
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:56,706
and settle almost instantly.

29
00:00:56,726 --> 00:00:58,976
People call this tokenisation.

30
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:01,037
Redbelly grew out of research

31
00:01:01,057 --> 00:01:04,357
at the University of Sydney and CSIRO,

32
00:01:04,377 --> 00:01:06,865
Australia's national science agency.

33
00:01:06,885 --> 00:01:08,745
And when the Reserve Bank of Australia

34
00:01:08,765 --> 00:01:11,085
trialled a pilot digital form

35
00:01:11,105 --> 00:01:14,505
of its own money, in Project Acacia,

36
00:01:14,525 --> 00:01:15,845
Redbelly was one of three

37
00:01:15,865 --> 00:01:17,915
platforms that carried it.

38
00:01:18,261 --> 00:01:19,694
Verified people.

39
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:21,139
Rules built in.

40
00:01:21,159 --> 00:01:22,889
Done in one step.

41
00:01:22,918 --> 00:01:24,368
That's Redbelly.
